                <pb facs="0823" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/367: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >McMillin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-26T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>26. Your March 22, 8 p.m.</p>
                <p>Arrangements have been made with Navy Department by which U.S.S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tacoma</hi> will be stationed for the present at San
                    José, Guatemala, and the U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Niagara</hi> at Puerto
                    Barrios, Guatemalan Minister here states he is informed all political prisoners
                    have been released, also that President Cabrera desires to accept Department’s
                    plan as outlined. Department desires further recommendations from you in regard
                    to the situation. Until further information is received from you, the Department
                    is unable to give further instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
